course: dictionary
lesson: 9760
title: Supply: one word, many jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: The word supply can be a verb (an action) or a noun (a thing). Its meaning depends on its job in the sentence. As a verb, to supply means to give or provide something people need. «Videos of people opening many loot boxes are sometimes paid for or supplied by the game company.» Supplied means provided: the company gives the videos.
explain: As a noun, a supply is an amount of something kept ready for when it is needed. Supplies are things like food, tools or school equipment. «Supply, weather and winter often stopped real campaigns altogether.» Here supply means the food, tools and other things an army needed, and the words around it show that it could run out.
explain: Use context clues to choose the right meaning. Ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence. In «a good blood supply», supply means the flow of blood that carries what the body needs to a wound. Blood supplies oxygen to the body, so supply means bringing something needed.
explain: Supply often goes with demand. «Supply and demand means how many people can do a job compared with how much people want it done; when lots of people can do a job, pay tends to be lower.» If you can use the clue words, you can work out the meaning without a dictionary.
fact: Supply can be a verb (to supply something) or a noun (a supply of something).
fact: «Supplied» means provided, given to people who need it.
fact: A supply is an amount kept ready for use when needed, such as an emergency supply of water and food.
fact: Supply and demand means how many people can do a job compared with how many people want it done.
fact: A supply chain is all the steps that bring goods to you.
exercise: «Videos of people opening many loot boxes are sometimes paid for or supplied by the game company.» What does supplied mean here? | Broken into pieces | Put away in a box | Stolen from the shop | *Provided, given to people
exercise: The school keeps a supply of pencils and paper for emergencies. What is a supply? | A thing you throw away | A teacher who gives lessons | *An amount kept ready for use | A type of school bus
exercise: «Wounds inside the mouth heal faster than wounds on the skin, helped by saliva and a good blood supply.» What does supply mean in this sentence? | A tool for cutting skin | *The flow of something the body needs | A loud noise | A kind of wound
test: Which word means the act of giving something people need? | *To supply | Supplies, in a bag | Demand | Supply
test: Which sentence uses supply as a noun, meaning an amount kept ready? | They were supplying the team with tools. | *The campers checked their emergency supply of water and food. | The shop will supply the school with paper. | Please supply your name.
exam: Which sentence uses supply as a verb? | Supplies were stored in the cupboard. | The supply of food was low. | *The company will supply the schools with paper. | A supply of water was kept in the tank.
